WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:05.050
<i>Line up by school. By school.</i>

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:09.100
<i>Teito Univesity. Saikyo University.</i>

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.090
<i>Tokyo Sport University.</i>

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.820
Starting in ten,

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:14.780
nine,

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:15.740
eight,

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:16.980
seven,

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:17.960
six,

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:18.940
five,

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:19.950
four,

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:20.960
three,

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:21.810
two,

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:22.460
one.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.680
Finish the first five kilometers in 3:10 each.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.590
After that, use your own judgment.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:01:01.950
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:39.760
Haiji!

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.940
Are you okay?

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.150
Are you hurt? Would you like to drop out?

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.250
You can do it!

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.340
You've got this!

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:03.430
Don't give up!

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.280
Hey, Hanako!

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:06.840
Dad.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.640
It's Musa and the twins.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:09.470
What?

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.710
The pack's starting to scatter.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:18.670
<b><i>Dreams and Reality</i></b>

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:25.330
<i>581 runners from 49 schools
are participating in this year's race.</i>

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:28.850
<i>Placing is determined by the total
time of a school's top ten finishers.</i>

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:36.250
<i>Of the 49 schools, the top ten will compete
at the New Year's Hakone Ekiden race.</i>

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:40.280
<i>As usual, the exchange
students are in the lead.</i>

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:44.030
I hope the runners behind
them don't get thrown off

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:47.450
and maintain their own pace instead.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.630
<i>The lead pack seems to have settled in.</i>

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.840
<i>The level of the qualifier rises every year.</i>

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.340
<i>We expect to see great
individual performances,</i>

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:06.260
<i>but in the qualifier, it's all about
the depth of a team's roster.</i>

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:12.030
<i>Every athlete hopes to finish
even one second faster.</i>

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:13.260
<i>Indeed.</i>

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:20.650
<b></b>

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:18.860
<i>It's raining steadily now.</i>

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:23.180
<i>In the qualifier for the Tokyo-Hakone
Collegiate Ekiden Relay Race,</i>

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:26.490
<i>the lead runners are approaching
the seven-kilometer mark.</i>

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.330
It's no use. I can't tell where Haiji is.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.520
He's probably in the lead pack.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:37.250
He managed to avoid getting
caught up in the fall, right?

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:37.950
Yeah.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:38.860
Seriously?

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:39.800
I don't know.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.880
The coach is confirming it right now.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.610
No way... He dropped out?

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:55.980
We'll head out onto the road, pass the station,

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.440
and cross under the monorail bridge.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.670
That's about ten kilometers.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.410
Ma'am!

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:11.620
Hana.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.700
Did you see everyone run by?

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:18.380
I caught glimpses of them,
but I didn't see them clearly.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.590
What about Haiji?

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:22.800
Haiji? I haven't seen him.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.190
Did something happen?

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:27.760
There! It's Haiji!

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:31.510
In the lead pack, behind Kakeru!

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:42.400
<i>They're moving.</i>

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:48.150
<i>The exchange students in the lead pack
are passing the ten-kilometer mark now.</i>

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:51.250
<i>Oka's Kipsuge is still in the front,</i>

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:54.990
<i>followed by Yakuo's Muskus and Saikyo's Jomo.</i>

00:05:54.990 --> 00:06:01.070
<i>Lagging behind are Kofu Academy's
Iwanki and Gaien's Ectoba.</i>

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.870
<i>After ten kilometers, use your own judgment.</i>

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.430
<i>Good luck.</i>

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:29.840
Hey.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.280
Are you watching?

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:37.170
Prince!

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:42.790
I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:06.610
<i>Kikui third-year Gunzawa and Tokyo Sport
fourth-year Takasugi are sprinting ahead.</i>

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:10.780
<i>As if it was planned,
the lead pack begins to shift</i>

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:13.050
<i>as they pass the ten-kilometer mark.</i>

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.360
<i>The two schools that tasted the
humiliation of losing their seeds last year</i>

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:21.420
<i>are trying to get a slight lead on the others.</i>

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.270
<i>No. Wait a minute.</i>

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:33.380
<i>Kansei University.</i>

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:36.860
<i>It's Kansei University
first-year Kurahara Kakeru.</i>

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:39.700
<i>Kansei University first-year
Kurahara Kakeru is sticking to—</i>

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:40.390
<i>No. Wait.</i>

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:42.370
<i>He's pulling ahead.</i>

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:45.810
<i>He's beaten the Kikui and Tokyo
Sport's burst of speed</i>

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.670
<i>and is now at the front of the lead pack.</i>

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:50.610
<i>Kurahara passed them.</i>

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:53.820
<i>Kurahara passed them just
before the turnaround point.</i>

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:10.010
<i>More.</i>

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:14.720
<i>More.</i>

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.180
<i>More!</i>

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:58.110
<i>Kurahara isn't stopping.</i>

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:04.250
<i>Kansei University first-year Kurahara Kakeru has passed Gaien second-year Ectoba</i>

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:09.690
<i>and is in a dead heat with Johann Iwanki, the monster of Hakone's section two.</i>

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:14.140
<i>Muskus and Jomo may be ahead
of them now, but they can't relax yet.</i>

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:17.180
I'm going to someplace
where I can see the finish line.

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:18.160
Be careful!

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:46.960
Go! Don't let him beat you!

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:48.310
You can catch them!

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.190
Excuse me. Sorry.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:18.790
I saw that guy at the track meet.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:29.440
Don't stop.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:32.120
Keep moving. Runners, to the field.

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:34.610
Less than an hour.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:35.620
They're fast.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:36.940
They're here!

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:47.280
Wow! He's keeping up with an exchange student!

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:48.740
He's up against Iwanki!

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:50.250
Keep it up, you two!

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:20.240
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Collegiate Ekiden Relay Race</b>

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:28.100
The runners are coming.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.710
Don't stop moving.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:36.510
Wow...

00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:38.340
Wow, wow, wow!

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:39.970
<i>Next runners are coming.</i>

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:15.740
King just finished.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.310
He's probably in the 120's.

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:21.270
Nico-chan Senpai.

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:26.110
Drink some water.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.200
Where's Prince?

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:40.010
You can do it!

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:41.460
The finish line's right there!

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:43.410
Your teammates are waiting!

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:46.380
You don't know that...

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:08.560
Sports aren't necessarily beautiful...

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:11.410
Get them out of here.

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:13.520
Keep moving them.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:14.410
Prince!

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:16.410
You're in the 100's!

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:17.870
You beat the 200's!

00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:23.750
Hey!

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:26.180
Why didn't you guys record your times?

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:28.930
Yuki, the camera's rolling.

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:33.410
It's all information warfare these days!

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:37.520
The race is more or less decided
before they announce the results!

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:41.860
You couldn't care less six months ago.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:44.110
If we average everyone's standing,

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:46.830
we probably come out around the mid-80's.

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:52.530
That's right on the
borderline of qualification.

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:17.930
I don't know what to say to them.

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:31.780
You ran well.

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:37.290
From far away, you're the only ones
who look like you're having a picnic.

00:15:37.810 --> 00:15:40.020
You've always got something to say.

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:53.530
We will now announce the results of the
Tokyo-Hakone Collegiate Ekiden Relay Race.

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:54.990
It's time.

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:02.730
First, Tokyo Sport University.

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:14.070
<b>Tokyo Sport University     10:09:12</b>

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:13.710
Damn.

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:16.280
They're under ten minutes.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:18.410
It was a high-paced race.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:21.340
Second.

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:23.630
Kofu Academy University.

00:16:25.990 --> 00:16:31.300
Seriously? They hesitated between
announcing the rank and school's name.

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:34.540
Third, Teito University.

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:40.960
We already know the results.
They should hurry it up.

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:43.200
Whining as soon as you've recovered?

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:45.040
You've got a lot of energy.

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:46.050
Fourth,

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:48.410
Kikui University.

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:56.160
Well, they've all been regulars so far.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:57.100
Fifth.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:01.580
<b>Tokyo Academy University</b>

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:01.090
Tokyo Academy University.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.880
Please, please, please, please.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.880
Come on, Kansei. Kansei.

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:06.720
Sixth,

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:08.830
Saikyo University.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.340
We didn't make it.

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:15.300
Seventh, Jonan Bunka University.

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:21.180
Eighth, Shinsei University.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:27.900
Ninth, Kanagawa International University.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:32.440
Tenth.

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:41.990
<b>Kansei University</b>

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:43.950
Kansei University.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.580
Yes!

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:57.300
Shindo!

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.510
Yeah!

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:07.440
All right!

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:18.160
Haiji!

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:43.640
<b>Kansei University     10:16:43</b>

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:45.880
It's not a mistake, is it?

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:49.100
It says tenth right there.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:50.890
It's like a TV show.

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:52.190
This is reality.

00:18:55.820 --> 00:19:00.950
Well, we proved that Hakone wasn't just a dream.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:06.300
All that's left is to train
and train until we reach the top.

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:08.370
We'll do nothing but practice
again starting tomorrow.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:12.340
Can't we have tomorrow off?

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:13.890
Let us rest!

00:19:13.890 --> 00:19:16.610
What more can we do?

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:20.130
I can't use this footage.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.700
Were you guys nervous getting water?

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:32.980
My heart was pounding.

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:33.980
I know what you mean.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:37.700
Oh, I know. Let's predict
which sections we'll run.

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:39.440
You're getting ahead of yourself.

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:41.650
I'm amazed you can read.

00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:43.660
I'm rewarding myself.

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:48.620
Guys, the fan club is giving us a gift of meat.

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.930
We're grilling meat tonight!

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:52.580
Yeah!

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:57.450
Hey, Kakeru.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:19:59.420
Kakeru.

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:04.830
Haiji said we'd reach the top.

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:06.630
Just now?

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:10.980
Just now, and when he recruited us to run.

00:20:12.460 --> 00:20:15.100
Let's aim for the top together!

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:17.710
He says it all the time.

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:20.440
And each time, I've thought, “yeah!”

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:22.500
And?

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:25.870
When he says top, do you think
he means winning the race?

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:33.210
Our total time was 10:16:43.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.580
Tokyo Sport, the top finisher in the qualifier,

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:37.290
was more than seven minutes faster.

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:42.430
Just how fast are the teams
that win the Hakone Ekiden?

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:46.090
Can we reach that level through practice?

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:54.050
Kakeru, what are we running for?

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:45.870
<b>Next time: Searching For the Answer</b>

00:22:40.530 --> 00:22:43.250
Next time: “Searching For the Answer.”
